WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.962
The book models a boundary as any
surface across which four things change.

2
00:00:04.962 --> 00:00:09.213
It's the book's own model, not a
FedRAMP or Microsoft construct.

3
00:00:09.213 --> 00:00:13.601
Telemetry fidelity asks which
signals actually arrive on this side.

4
00:00:13.601 --> 00:00:16.539
In GCC, admin-center network connectivity,

5
00:00:16.539 --> 00:00:21.912
informed network routing and Adoption
Score are documented as unavailable.

6
00:00:21.912 --> 00:00:26.358
Identity authority asks who
a claim's issuer resolves to:

7
00:00:26.358 --> 00:00:32.788
GCC pairs with Entra ID in commercial Azure,
GCC High and DoD with Azure Government.

8
00:00:32.788 --> 00:00:37.975
Enforcement responsibility asks who must
enforce a control: without Microsoft's

9
00:00:37.975 --> 00:00:43.163
per-circuit feedback, path selection rests
on the agency's own SD-WAN measurements.

10
00:00:43.163 --> 00:00:45.784
Provenance classification asks whether a

11
00:00:45.784 --> 00:00:48.551
claim is still authoritative,
or only derived.

12
00:00:48.551 --> 00:00:51.475
Each dimension raises its own drift class.

13
00:00:51.475 --> 00:00:56.650
Detection is shipped for two classes,
partial for one and design only for two.

14
00:00:56.650 --> 00:00:59.697
And FedRAMP's definition
of federal customer data

15
00:00:59.697 --> 00:01:03.325
excludes the analytics and
telemetry a provider generates.

16
00:01:03.325 --> 00:01:05.900
No certification promises you a signal.
